NNAAMMEE
       pamtouil  -  convert  a  PNM or PNM/transparency image into a Motif UIL
       icon file


SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ppaammttoouuiill [--nnaammee==_u_i_l_n_a_m_e] [_p_a_m_f_i_l_e]

       You may abbreviate any option to its shortest unique prefix.   You  may
       use  two hyphens instead of one to delimit an option.  You may separate
       an option from its value with whitespace instead of ==.


DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       ppaammttoouuiill reads a PNM or PAM image as input and  produces  a  Motif  UIL
       icon  file  as output.  If the input is PAM, it may be either a regular
       grayscale or color image or grayscale+transparency  or  color+transpar‐
       ency.  Where the transparency channel is present, ppaammttoouuiill renders pix‐
       els that are more than half transparent as transparent in the output.

       In the UIL's colormap, ppaammttoouuiill uses the color names from the RGB data‐
       base  -- the same one ppppmmmmaakkee(1) uses.  Where a color in the input does
       not exactly match one of the colors named in the RGB database, ppaammttoouuiill
       uses the closest color named in the RGB database.


OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       In  addition  to  the options common to all programs based on libnetpbm
       (most notably --qquuiieett, see
        Common Options ⟨index.html#commonoptions⟩ ), ppaammttoouuiill  recognizes  the
       following command line option:




       --nnaammee
                   Allows you to specify the prefix string which is printed in
              the
                   resulting UIL output.  If not specified,  will  default  to
              the filename
                   (without  extension)  of the ppmfile argument.  If --nnaammee is
              not
                   specified and no ppmfile is specified (i.e.  piped  input),
              the
                   prefix string will default to the string "noname".




